IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wrongs-core`

-- Wrongs Act 1958 (Vic) -- the seat of the person who was injured or harmed (the claimant, the plaintiff), and, in
-- Parts XIII and XIIIA, the person who was abused as a child. Each question is asked as that person would ask it,
-- with plain inputs; the rules are in wrongs-core.l4 and none is restated here. Judgments the Act leaves to a court
-- (reasonable, satisfied, just, akin to an employee) are asked as "would a court find ...", never decided.
-- Every question assumes a proceeding commenced on or after 1 January 2004 (see NOTES.md, Scope).
-- BASELINE, not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Wrongs Act 1958 (Vic) -- questions for the injured person`

§§ `Personal injury damages: the caps (Part VB)`
-- Situation: you are claiming damages for an injury (or a death) caused by someone else's fault.

@export Does Part VB of the Wrongs Act 1958 (Vic) -- the caps and limits on personal injury damages -- apply to my award (s 28C)? Answers nothing if the damages are not for death or injury caused by another person's fault.
GIVEN `my damages are for death or injury caused by another person's fault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming damages for an injury to you (or a death) caused by the act or omission of someone else?
      `the fault was intentional harm or sexual misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fault an intentional act done to cause death or injury, or sexual assault or other sexual misconduct?
      `my award comes under` IS A `Scheme` @desc Does the award come under another law: the Transport Accident Act 1986 (Parts 3, 6, 10), the Accident Compensation Act 1985 Part IV, the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 Part 5 or Part 7, the Workers Compensation Act 1958, emergency, police, juries or education compensation, victims of crime assistance (1996 or 2022 Act), the Equal Opportunity Act 2010, a superannuation or insurance payment; or none?
      `my award is of a class excluded by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the award of a class the Wrongs regulations exclude from Part VB? (Answer no unless told otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does Part VB apply to my award of personal injury damages` `my damages are for death or injury caused by another person's fault` `the fault was intentional harm or sexual misconduct` `my award comes under` `my award is of a class excluded by regulations` MEANS
    `s 28C -- Part VB applies to the award` `my damages are for death or injury caused by another person's fault` `the fault was intentional harm or sexual misconduct` `my award comes under` `my award is of a class excluded by regulations`

@export What is the most I can be awarded for each week of lost earnings, lost earning capacity or lost financial support (s 28F)? Three times average weekly earnings at the date of the award, where Part VB applies.
GIVEN `average weekly earnings in Victoria` IS A NUMBER @desc The Australian Statistician's latest estimate, before the date of the award, of average weekly total earnings of all employees in Victoria, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be awarded for each week of lost earnings` `average weekly earnings in Victoria` MEANS
    `s 28F -- the weekly maximum for loss of earnings` `average weekly earnings in Victoria`

@export What is the most I can be awarded for non-economic loss (pain and suffering, loss of amenities and enjoyment of life) (ss 28G, 28H)? Answers nothing for an award outside 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027, the years whose figures are encoded.
GIVEN `the day of the award` IS A DATE @desc The day the damages are (or would be) awarded (ISO date, e.g. 2026-09-01)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most I can be awarded for non-economic loss` `the day of the award` MEANS
    `s 28G, s 28H -- the maximum for non-economic loss` `the day of the award`

@export What discount rate is used to bring my future economic loss to a lump sum (s 28I)? The rate prescribed by the regulations, or 5 per cent if none is prescribed.
GIVEN `a discount rate is prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Wrongs regulations prescribe a discount rate percentage? (Answer no unless you know one is prescribed.)
      `the prescribed rate` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the prescribed percentage (5 means 5 per cent; any number otherwise)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What discount rate applies to my future economic loss` `a discount rate is prescribed by regulations` `the prescribed rate` MEANS
    `s 28I -- the discount rate` `a discount rate is prescribed by regulations` `the prescribed rate`

@export Can I be awarded damages for unpaid care that family or friends give me because of my injury (gratuitous attendant care, s 28IA)?
GIVEN `a court would find a reasonable need for the care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court be satisfied there is (or was) a reasonable need for the care to be provided?
      `the need arose solely because of my injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the need arisen solely because of the injury?
      `I would not get the care but for my injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the care not be (or have been) provided to you but for the injury?
      `hours of care per week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week the care is (or is to be) provided
      `months of care` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months the care is (or is to be) provided
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I be awarded damages for gratuitous attendant care` `a court would find a reasonable need for the care` `the need arose solely because of my injury` `I would not get the care but for my injury` `hours of care per week` `months of care` MEANS
    `s 28IA -- damages for gratuitous attendant care may be awarded` `a court would find a reasonable need for the care` `the need arose solely because of my injury` `I would not get the care but for my injury` `hours of care per week` `months of care`

@export What is the most I can be awarded per week for gratuitous attendant care (s 28IB)? At 40 hours a week or more, average weekly earnings; under 40 hours, one-fortieth of it for each hour.
GIVEN `hours of care per week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week the care is (or is to be) provided
      `average weekly total earnings in Victoria for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc The Australian Statistician's average weekly total earnings of all employees in Victoria for the period of the care, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be awarded per week for gratuitous attendant care` `hours of care per week` `average weekly total earnings in Victoria for the period` MEANS
    `ss 28IB, 28IE -- the weekly maximum for care` `hours of care per week` `average weekly total earnings in Victoria for the period`

@export Can I be awarded damages because my injury stops me caring, unpaid, for my dependants (s 28ID, s 28IF)?
GIVEN `my dependants are` IS A `Kind of dependant` @desc Are the dependants people who depended on you (wholly, mainly or in part) when the liability arose, or your unborn children at that time who were born after it?
      `I cared for them before the liability arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For dependants who already depended on you: did you provide the care before the liability arose?
      `they cannot care for themselves because of age or incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are (or will) the dependants be unable to provide the care themselves because of their age or physical or mental incapacity?
      `hours per week I would have cared` IS A NUMBER @desc But for the injury, how many hours a week would you reasonably be expected to have provided the care?
      `consecutive months I would have cared` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive months?
      `a court would find the need will exist and is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court be satisfied the care will be needed for those hours and that period, and that the need is reasonable?
      `the dependant has already recovered damages for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the dependant already recovered damages for this loss of your capacity to care?
      `my injury is a dust disease or from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your injury a dust-related condition (for example asbestos disease) or from smoking, tobacco products or tobacco smoke?
      `my claim is about a health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your claim relate to the provision of, or a failure to provide, a health service?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I be awarded damages for loss of my capacity to care for my dependants` `my dependants are` `I cared for them before the liability arose` `they cannot care for themselves because of age or incapacity` `hours per week I would have cared` `consecutive months I would have cared` `a court would find the need will exist and is reasonable` `the dependant has already recovered damages for it` `my injury is a dust disease or from tobacco` `my claim is about a health service` MEANS
    `s 28ID -- damages for loss of capacity to care for dependants may be awarded` `my dependants are` `I cared for them before the liability arose` `they cannot care for themselves because of age or incapacity` `hours per week I would have cared` `consecutive months I would have cared` `a court would find the need will exist and is reasonable` `the dependant has already recovered damages for it` (`s 28IF -- the dust or tobacco exception applies` `my injury is a dust disease or from tobacco` `my claim is about a health service`)

@export What is the most I can be awarded per week for loss of my capacity to care for my dependants (s 28IE)? Answers nothing for a dust disease or tobacco claim not about a health service, where s 28IE does not apply (s 28IF).
GIVEN `hours per week I would have cared` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week the court is satisfied you would have provided the care
      `average weekly total earnings in Victoria for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc The Australian Statistician's average weekly total earnings of all employees in Victoria for the period, in dollars
      `my injury is a dust disease or from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your injury a dust-related condition or from smoking, tobacco products or tobacco smoke?
      `my claim is about a health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your claim relate to the provision of, or a failure to provide, a health service?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most I can be awarded per week for loss of my capacity to care` `hours per week I would have cared` `average weekly total earnings in Victoria for the period` `my injury is a dust disease or from tobacco` `my claim is about a health service` MEANS
    IF `s 28IF -- the dust or tobacco exception applies` `my injury is a dust disease or from tobacco` `my claim is about a health service`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`ss 28IB, 28IE -- the weekly maximum for care` `hours per week I would have cared` `average weekly total earnings in Victoria for the period`)

§§ `Damages for non-economic loss: the significant injury threshold (Part VBA)`
-- Situation: you are claiming damages for pain and suffering or loss of enjoyment of life for an injury.

@export Does my degree of permanent impairment satisfy the threshold level (s 28LB)? More than 5 per cent for most injuries, 5 per cent or more for a spinal injury, 10 per cent or more for a psychiatric injury.
GIVEN `my injury is` IS A `Kind of injury` @desc Is the injury a psychiatric injury, a spinal injury, or another injury?
      `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your whole person permanent impairment, in per cent, as assessed under the A.M.A. Guides (4th edition) as modified by Part VBA
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does my impairment satisfy the threshold level` `my injury is` `my degree of impairment` MEANS
    `s 28LB -- the degree of impairment satisfies the threshold level` `my injury is` `my degree of impairment`

@export What degree of impairment is assessed for my binaural hearing loss (s 28LK)? Zero at 5 per cent NAL or less; above that, the percentage itself.
GIVEN `my binaural hearing loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Your binaural loss of hearing, in per cent NAL, determined under the National Acoustic Laboratory's Improved Procedure
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What degree of impairment is assessed for my hearing loss` `my binaural hearing loss` MEANS
    `s 28LK -- the degree of impairment for hearing loss` `my binaural hearing loss`

@export Is my injury a significant injury for Part VBA (s 28LF, s 28LZH)?
GIVEN `my injury is psychiatric` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the injury a psychiatric injury?
      `the Medical Panel's determination` IS A `Medical Panel determination` @desc Has a Medical Panel determined whether your impairment satisfies the threshold level: no determination, satisfied, or not satisfied?
      `an approved medical practitioner certified I meet the threshold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an approved medical practitioner assessed your impairment as satisfying the threshold level (a s 28LN certificate of assessment)?
      `I have a certificate that I will meet the threshold once stable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a certificate been issued under s 28LNA (the injury has not stabilised but will satisfy the threshold once it does)?
      `my injury is loss of a foetus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the injury the loss of a foetus?
      `my injury is psychological harm from losing a child at birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it psychological or psychiatric injury from the loss of a child because of an injury to the mother, foetus or child before, during or immediately after the birth?
      `my injury is loss of a breast` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the injury the loss of a breast?
      `the respondent agreed to waive the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent you are asking about agreed in writing, under Division 4, to waive the assessment because the injury is significant? (An agreement binds only that respondent.)
      `the Panel's certificate deems it significant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a Medical Panel certified that your impairment will satisfy the threshold once stable (s 28LZG(5)), or that it still cannot decide 12 months after the first assessment (s 28LZGA(4))?
      `a court determined significant injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court determined significant injury under s 28LZN (imminent death, or a claim surviving for an estate)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my injury a significant injury` `my injury is psychiatric` `the Medical Panel's determination` `an approved medical practitioner certified I meet the threshold` `I have a certificate that I will meet the threshold once stable` `my injury is loss of a foetus` `my injury is psychological harm from losing a child at birth` `my injury is loss of a breast` `the respondent agreed to waive the assessment` `the Panel's certificate deems it significant` `a court determined significant injury` MEANS
    `s 28LF -- the injury is significant injury` `my injury is psychiatric` `the Medical Panel's determination` `an approved medical practitioner certified I meet the threshold` `I have a certificate that I will meet the threshold once stable` `my injury is loss of a foetus` `my injury is psychological harm from losing a child at birth` `my injury is loss of a breast` `the respondent agreed to waive the assessment` `the Panel's certificate deems it significant` `a court determined significant injury`

@export Can I recover damages for non-economic loss, or does Part VBA's significant injury threshold stop me (ss 28LC, 28LE)? Answers nothing where Part VBA does not apply (another law, such as the Transport Accident Act or the workers' compensation Acts, has its own threshold).
GIVEN `the fault was intentional harm or sexual misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fault an intentional act done to cause death or injury, or sexual assault or other sexual misconduct?
      `my claim comes under` IS A `Scheme` @desc Does your claim come under another law (the Transport Accident Act 1986 Parts 3, 6, 10; the Accident Compensation Act 1985 Part IV; the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 Part 5; the Workers Compensation Act 1958; or another), or none?
      `my injury is an asbestos-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your injury an asbestos-related condition?
      `my claim is of a class excluded by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim of a class the regulations exclude from Part VBA? (Answer no unless told otherwise.)
      `my injury is a significant injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your injury a significant injury (see the significant injury question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I recover damages for non-economic loss under Part VBA` `the fault was intentional harm or sexual misconduct` `my claim comes under` `my injury is an asbestos-related condition` `my claim is of a class excluded by regulations` `my injury is a significant injury` MEANS
    `s 28LE -- damages for non-economic loss can be recovered` (`s 28LC -- Part VBA applies to the claim` `the fault was intentional harm or sexual misconduct` `my claim comes under` `my injury is an asbestos-related condition` `my claim is of a class excluded by regulations`) `my injury is a significant injury`

@export Can I ask the court itself to determine that my injury is significant, without the usual assessment (s 28LZN)?
GIVEN `my claim is urgent because I am expected to die soon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Should the claim be dealt with urgently because of your imminent death?
      `the claim survives for an estate and the person died of something else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a claim brought for an estate under s 29(1) of the Administration and Probate Act 1958: did the person die from a cause other than the injury?
      `a court would find the injury significant if assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court be satisfied the injury, if assessed under Division 3, would be (or would have been) significant injury?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the court determine that my injury is significant` `my claim is urgent because I am expected to die soon` `the claim survives for an estate and the person died of something else` `a court would find the injury significant if assessed` MEANS
    `s 28LZN -- the court may determine significant injury` `my claim is urgent because I am expected to die soon` `the claim survives for an estate and the person died of something else` `a court would find the injury significant if assessed`

§§ `The steps with the respondent (Part VBA Division 4)`
-- Situation: you have asked the respondent to waive the assessment, or served a certificate of assessment.

@export By what day must the respondent answer my written request to waive the impairment assessment (s 28LO(2))? If it does not answer by then, it cannot waive the assessment (s 28LO(4)).
GIVEN `the day the respondent received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day the respondent received your written request (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must the respondent answer my waiver request` `the day the respondent received my request` MEANS
    `Division 4 -- the last day of 60 days after receipt` `the day the respondent received my request`

@export The respondent says it is not the proper respondent: by what day must I give it my written notice (s 28LQ(1), s 28LWB(1))?
GIVEN `the day I received its response` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the respondent's response (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I reply to a respondent who says it is not the proper respondent` `the day I received its response` MEANS
    `Division 4 -- the last day of 14 days after receipt` `the day I received its response`

@export By what day must the respondent respond to the certificate of assessment I served (s 28LW(1))?
GIVEN `the day the respondent received my certificate and the information` IS A DATE @desc The day the respondent received both the certificate of assessment and the information required by s 28LT (the later of the two; ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must the respondent respond to my certificate of assessment` `the day the respondent received my certificate and the information` MEANS
    `Division 4 -- the last day of 60 days after receipt` `the day the respondent received my certificate and the information`

@export Has the respondent accepted my assessment, or is it taken to have accepted it (ss 28LW, 28LWE)?
GIVEN `the day the respondent received my certificate and the information` IS A DATE @desc The day the respondent received both the certificate of assessment and the information required by s 28LT (ISO date)
      `the respondent responded in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent responded to you in writing?
      `the day of its response` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it responded (ISO date; any date otherwise)
      `its response` IS A `Response to a certificate` @desc What it said: accepts the assessment, will refer a medical question to a Medical Panel, needs further information, or is not the proper respondent (any choice if it has not responded)
      `it referred the question to a Medical Panel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it referred a medical question about the assessment to a Medical Panel?
      `the day it referred the question` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it referred it (ISO date; any date otherwise)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH AN `Assessment status`
`Has the respondent accepted my assessment` `the day the respondent received my certificate and the information` `the respondent responded in writing` `the day of its response` `its response` `it referred the question to a Medical Panel` `the day it referred the question` `today` MEANS
    `s 28LW, s 28LWE -- the status of the assessment` `the day the respondent received my certificate and the information` `the respondent responded in writing` `the day of its response` `its response` `it referred the question to a Medical Panel` `the day it referred the question` `today`

@export Until what day is my limitation period suspended after I served a certificate of assessment (s 28LV)? Three months after the first of: acceptance, deemed acceptance, the end of the time to challenge a Medical Panel's determination, or the final determination of a challenge.
GIVEN `the day the first of those events happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the first of those events happened (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`Until what day is my limitation period suspended` `the day the first of those events happened` MEANS
    `s 28LV -- the limitation period is suspended until` `the day the first of those events happened`

§§ `Negligence (Part X) and mental harm (Part XI)`
-- Situation: you are claiming damages for harm caused by someone's negligence.

@export Do Parts X (negligence) and XI (mental harm) of the Wrongs Act 1958 apply to my claim (ss 44, 45, 68, 69)? Answers nothing if the claim is not for damages resulting from negligence.
GIVEN `my claim is for damages resulting from negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for damages resulting from a failure to take reasonable care (in tort, contract, under a statute or otherwise)?
      `my claim comes under` IS A `Scheme` @desc Does your claim come under another law (transport accident, workers' compensation, emergency, police, juries or education compensation, or another), or none?
      `my injury is a dust disease or from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your injury a dust-related condition (for example asbestos disease) or from smoking, tobacco products or tobacco smoke?
      `my claim is about a health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your claim relate to the provision of, or a failure to provide, a health service?
      `my claim is of a class excluded by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim of a class the regulations exclude from Parts X and XI? (Answer no unless told otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do Parts X and XI apply to my claim` `my claim is for damages resulting from negligence` `my claim comes under` `my injury is a dust disease or from tobacco` `my claim is about a health service` `my claim is of a class excluded by regulations` MEANS
    `ss 45, 69 -- Parts X and XI apply to the claim` `my claim is for damages resulting from negligence` `my claim comes under` `my injury is a dust disease or from tobacco` `my claim is about a health service` `my claim is of a class excluded by regulations`

@export Could the other person have been negligent in failing to take precautions against the risk that harmed me (s 48(1))? No unless the risk was foreseeable, not insignificant, and a reasonable person would have taken the precautions.
GIVEN `the risk was foreseeable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the other person know, or ought they to have known, of the risk?
      `the risk was not insignificant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the risk not insignificant (more than far-fetched or fanciful)?
      `a court would find a reasonable person would have taken the precautions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court find that a reasonable person in their position would have taken those precautions (weighing probability, seriousness, burden and social utility, s 48(2))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Could the other person have been negligent in failing to take precautions` `the risk was foreseeable` `the risk was not insignificant` `a court would find a reasonable person would have taken the precautions` MEANS
    `s 48(1) -- the person can be negligent in failing to take the precautions` `the risk was foreseeable` `the risk was not insignificant` `a court would find a reasonable person would have taken the precautions`

@export Did the negligence cause my harm (s 51)? It must be a necessary condition of the harm (or taken as one by the court in an appropriate case), and within the scope of liability. You bear the burden of proof (s 52).
GIVEN `the harm would not have happened without the negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the negligence a necessary condition of the harm?
      `a court would take factual causation as established anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not: would the court, in an exceptional case under s 51(2), take factual causation as established?
      `a court would find liability should extend to my harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court find it appropriate for the negligent person's liability to extend to the harm (scope of liability)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Did the negligence cause my harm` `the harm would not have happened without the negligence` `a court would take factual causation as established anyway` `a court would find liability should extend to my harm` MEANS
    `s 51 -- the negligence caused the harm` `the harm would not have happened without the negligence` `a court would take factual causation as established anyway` `a court would find liability should extend to my harm`

@export The other side says I voluntarily took the risk: am I presumed to have known of it (ss 53, 54)? Answers nothing for a professional or health service, or work done for another, where the common law applies.
GIVEN `the other side raises voluntary assumption of risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other side raise the defence of voluntary assumption of risk (volenti non fit injuria)?
      `the risk would have been obvious to a reasonable person in my position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the risk have been obvious to a reasonable person in your position (patent or a matter of common knowledge, even if unlikely or not visible)?
      `the risk came from a thing not being properly maintained or cared for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the risk created by someone failing to properly operate, maintain, replace, prepare or care for a thing (including an animal), where that failure was not itself obvious?
      `my claim is about a professional or health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your claim relate to the provision of, or a failure to provide, a professional or health service?
      `my claim is about the risks of work I did for another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim about risks associated with work done by one person for another?
      `I can prove I was not aware of the risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove, on the balance of probabilities, that you were not aware of the risk?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I presumed to have been aware of the risk` `the other side raises voluntary assumption of risk` `the risk would have been obvious to a reasonable person in my position` `the risk came from a thing not being properly maintained or cared for` `my claim is about a professional or health service` `my claim is about the risks of work I did for another` `I can prove I was not aware of the risk` MEANS
    `s 54 -- I am presumed to have been aware of the risk` `the other side raises voluntary assumption of risk` `the risk would have been obvious to a reasonable person in my position` `the risk came from a thing not being properly maintained or cared for` `my claim is about a professional or health service` `my claim is about the risks of work I did for another` `I can prove I was not aware of the risk`

@export Is the other side free of liability because my harm came from an inherent risk, one that reasonable care could not avoid (s 55)? Not where the claim is about a duty to warn.
GIVEN `my harm came from a risk reasonable care could not avoid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the harm come from a risk of something occurring that could not be avoided by the exercise of reasonable care?
      `my claim is about a duty to warn of the risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim in connection with a duty to warn of the risk?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the other side not liable because the risk was inherent` `my harm came from a risk reasonable care could not avoid` `my claim is about a duty to warn of the risk` MEANS
    `s 55 -- the defendant is not liable because the risk was inherent` `my harm came from a risk reasonable care could not avoid` `my claim is about a duty to warn of the risk`

@export I say I was not warned or not told: must I prove I was not aware of the risk or information (s 56)? Answers nothing for work done for another (unless about a health service), where the common law applies.
GIVEN `I allege I was not warned or not given information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you allege the other side failed to warn you of a risk, or failed to give you other information?
      `my claim is about the risks of work I did for another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim about risks associated with work done by one person for another?
      `my claim is about a health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proceeding relate to the provision of, or a failure to provide, a health service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I prove I was not aware of the risk` `I allege I was not warned or not given information` `my claim is about the risks of work I did for another` `my claim is about a health service` MEANS
    `s 56 -- I must prove I was not aware of the risk` `I allege I was not warned or not given information` `my claim is about the risks of work I did for another` `my claim is about a health service`

@export Can the professional I am suing escape a finding of negligence because they acted as widely accepted peer professional opinion (ss 59, 60)? Answers nothing if it is not a professional service, or the claim is about a warning or information about a risk.
GIVEN `I am suing a professional for a professional service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you are suing an individual practising a profession, sued for a professional service?
      `my claim is about a warning or information about a risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim about giving, or failing to give, a warning or information about a risk?
      `they acted as widely accepted peer professional opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they act in a manner widely accepted in Australia, at the time, by a significant number of respected practitioners in the field as competent practice?
      `a court would find that opinion unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court find that peer professional opinion unreasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the professional rely on peer professional opinion` `I am suing a professional for a professional service` `my claim is about a warning or information about a risk` `they acted as widely accepted peer professional opinion` `a court would find that opinion unreasonable` MEANS
    `s 59 -- the professional is not negligent because of peer professional opinion` `I am suing a professional for a professional service` `my claim is about a warning or information about a risk` `they acted as widely accepted peer professional opinion` `a court would find that opinion unreasonable`

@export How much can I recover if I was partly at fault myself (contributory negligence, s 26, s 63)? The court reduces the damages by the share it thinks just and equitable (up to 100 per cent, which defeats the claim). Dependants suing for a death are not reduced for the deceased's own fault.
GIVEN `my total damages` IS A NUMBER @desc The total damages that would be awarded if you had not been at fault, in dollars
      `the reduction a court would think just` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage reduction the court thinks just and equitable for your share in the responsibility (0 to 100)
      `we are dependants suing for a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this an action by dependants under Part III of the Wrongs Act for the death of a person who was partly at fault?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much can I recover after contributory negligence` `my total damages` `the reduction a court would think just` `we are dependants suing for a death` MEANS
    `s 26, s 63 -- the damages after contributory negligence` `my total damages` `the reduction a court would think just` `we are dependants suing for a death`

@export Could the other person have owed me a duty not to cause me pure mental harm (mental harm not from an injury of my own) (s 72)?
GIVEN `they ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they foresee, or ought they to have foreseen, that a person of normal fortitude might, in the circumstances, suffer a recognised psychiatric illness if reasonable care were not taken?
      `they knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they know, or ought they to have known, that you are a person of less than normal fortitude?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Could I have been owed a duty not to be caused pure mental harm` `they ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a psychiatric illness` `they knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude` MEANS
    `s 72 -- a duty not to cause me pure mental harm is not ruled out` `they ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a psychiatric illness` `they knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude`

@export I suffered mental harm from the shock of someone else being killed, injured or put in danger: does s 73 let me recover damages? Answers nothing if the harm did not arise from such a shock.
GIVEN `my harm arose from shock at someone being killed, injured or endangered by them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your mental harm arise wholly or partly from mental or nervous shock at another person (the victim) being killed, injured or put in danger by the defendant?
      `I witnessed it at the scene` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you witness, at the scene, the victim being killed, injured or put in danger?
      `I am or was close to the victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or were you, in a close relationship with the victim?
      `the victim could not recover damages for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the victim's own recovery of damages from the defendant for the act or omission be prevented by any law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does s 73 let me recover damages for mental harm from shock` `my harm arose from shock at someone being killed, injured or endangered by them` `I witnessed it at the scene` `I am or was close to the victim` `the victim could not recover damages for it` MEANS
    `s 73 -- s 73 allows damages for pure mental harm from shock` `my harm arose from shock at someone being killed, injured or endangered by them` `I witnessed it at the scene` `I am or was close to the victim` `the victim could not recover damages for it`

@export Can I recover damages for mental harm that followed from my own injury (consequential mental harm, s 74)?
GIVEN `they ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the defendant foresee, or ought they to have foreseen, that a person of normal fortitude might, in the circumstances (including your injury), suffer a recognised psychiatric illness if reasonable care were not taken?
      `they knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they know, or ought they to have known, that you are a person of less than normal fortitude?
      `they ought to have foreseen I might suffer a psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they foresee, or ought they to have foreseen, that you might suffer a recognised psychiatric illness if reasonable care were not taken?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I recover damages for consequential mental harm` `they ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a psychiatric illness` `they knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude` `they ought to have foreseen I might suffer a psychiatric illness` MEANS
    `s 74 -- damages for consequential mental harm can be recovered` `they ought to have foreseen a person of normal fortitude might suffer a psychiatric illness` `they knew or ought to have known I am of less than normal fortitude` `they ought to have foreseen I might suffer a psychiatric illness`

@export Can I be awarded damages for economic loss (such as lost earnings) for mental harm from negligence (s 75)? Only if the harm is a recognised psychiatric illness.
GIVEN `my mental harm is a recognised psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your mental harm consist of a recognised psychiatric illness?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I be awarded economic loss damages for mental harm` `my mental harm is a recognised psychiatric illness` MEANS
    `s 75 -- damages for economic loss for mental harm can be awarded` `my mental harm is a recognised psychiatric illness`

§§ `Proportionate liability (Part IVAA)`
-- Situation: you are claiming economic loss or property damage (not an injury) from two or more wrongdoers.

@export Is my claim an apportionable claim, so that each wrongdoer pays only its share (ss 24AF, 24AG)? Answers nothing for a claim that is neither for economic loss or property damage from a failure to take reasonable care, nor under s 18 of the Australian Consumer Law.
GIVEN `my claim is for` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc Is your claim for economic loss or damage to property from a failure to take reasonable care, for damages for misleading or deceptive conduct under s 18 of the Australian Consumer Law (Victoria), or something else?
      `my claim arises out of an injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claim arise out of a personal injury (including psychological injury or disease)?
      `my claim comes under` IS A `Scheme` @desc Does the claim come under another law (transport accident, workers' compensation, emergency or police compensation, victims of crime assistance, the Equal Opportunity Act 2010, juries or education compensation), or none?
      `my claim is of a class excluded by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim of a class the regulations exclude from Part IVAA? (Answer no unless told otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my claim an apportionable claim` `my claim is for` `my claim arises out of an injury` `my claim comes under` `my claim is of a class excluded by regulations` MEANS
    `ss 24AF, 24AG -- the claim is an apportionable claim` `my claim is for` `my claim arises out of an injury` `my claim comes under` `my claim is of a class excluded by regulations`

@export On an apportionable claim, what is the most I can get judgment for against one defendant (ss 24AI, 24AM)? Its just share of my loss; all the defendants' shares if a finding of fraud is made against it. Answers nothing if it is not a concurrent wrongdoer.
GIVEN `my loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The loss or damage claimed, in dollars
      `the defendant is one of two or more who caused my loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant one of two or more persons whose acts or omissions caused the loss, independently or jointly (a concurrent wrongdoer)?
      `its share a court would think just` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of the loss the court considers just for that defendant's responsibility
      `the other defendants' shares` IS A NUMBER @desc The total percentage the court gives the other defendants in the same proceeding
      `the court finds it acted fraudulently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a finding of fraud made against that defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most I can get judgment for against one defendant` `my loss` `the defendant is one of two or more who caused my loss` `its share a court would think just` `the other defendants' shares` `the court finds it acted fraudulently` MEANS
    `s 24AI, s 24AM -- the most judgment can be given for against the defendant` `my loss` `the defendant is one of two or more who caused my loss` `its share a court would think just` `the other defendants' shares` `the court finds it acted fraudulently`

@export I already have judgment against one wrongdoer: what is the most I can recover from another in a later action (s 24AK)?
GIVEN `my loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The loss or damage you actually suffered, in dollars
      `what I have already recovered` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages you have already recovered for that loss, in dollars
      `its share a court would think just` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of the loss the court considers just for the other wrongdoer's responsibility
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can recover from another wrongdoer later` `my loss` `what I have already recovered` `its share a court would think just` MEANS
    `s 24AK -- the most I can recover in a later action` `my loss` `what I have already recovered` `its share a court would think just`

§§ `Child abuse in an organisation (Part XIII)`
-- Situation: you were abused as a child by someone connected with an organisation that had care of you.

@export Is the organisation a "relevant organisation" that owes children the Part XIII duty (s 88)?
GIVEN `it is the State of Victoria itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity the State of Victoria itself?
      `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an entity organised for some end, purpose or work (a school, club, church, charity, business, agency and the like)?
      `it has care, supervision or authority over children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it exercise care, supervision or authority over children, as part of its main activities or otherwise?
      `its legal standing` IS A `Legal standing of the entity` @desc Can it be sued; or has it nominated a legal person to be sued; or is it an NGO that can be sued under the Legal Identity of Defendants Act 2018, a statutory office holder, a Department or Administrative Office, a public body corporate, or Victoria Police; or none of these?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the organisation a relevant organisation` `it is the State of Victoria itself` `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` `it has care, supervision or authority over children` `its legal standing` MEANS
    `s 88 -- the entity is a relevant organisation` `it is the State of Victoria itself` `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` `it has care, supervision or authority over children` `its legal standing`

@export Was the person who abused me "associated" with the organisation (s 90)? Answers nothing for a role the open list does not name.
GIVEN `the abuser was` IS AN `Abuser's role` @desc Was the abuser an officer, office holder, employee, owner, volunteer or contractor; a minister, religious leader, officer or member of personnel of a religious organisation; such a person of an organisation the care was delegated to; the specified carer (foster or kinship carer) the care was delegated to, with or without a permanent care order; or someone else?
      `the organisation is religious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the organisation a religious organisation?
      `the only link is that the organisation funded or regulated another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only link that the organisation wholly or partly funds or regulates another organisation the abuser was part of?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was the abuser associated with the organisation` `the abuser was` `the organisation is religious` `the only link is that the organisation funded or regulated another` MEANS
    `s 90 -- the individual is associated with the organisation` `the abuser was` `the organisation is religious` `the only link is that the organisation funded or regulated another`

@export Is the organisation presumed to have breached its duty to prevent my abuse, unless it proves it took reasonable precautions (s 91)? Answers nothing for abuse before 1 July 2017 (Part XIII does not apply) or an abuser whose association the Act's open list does not settle.
GIVEN `the day of the abuse` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse happened (or began; ISO date)
      `my age at the abuse` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age, in years, when the abuse happened
      `the abuse was` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc Was it sexual assault or other sexual misconduct, physical abuse, force with a lawful justification or excuse, or other harm?
      `it is the State of Victoria itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity the State of Victoria itself?
      `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the organisation an entity organised for some end, purpose or work?
      `it has care, supervision or authority over children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it exercise care, supervision or authority over children?
      `its legal standing` IS A `Legal standing of the entity` @desc Its legal standing (see the relevant organisation question)
      `the abuser was` IS AN `Abuser's role` @desc The abuser's role (see the association question)
      `the organisation is religious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the organisation a religious organisation?
      `the only link is that the organisation funded or regulated another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only link that the organisation funds or regulates another organisation?
      `I was in its care, supervision or authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under the organisation's care, supervision or authority when the abuse happened?
      `the abuse was wholly unrelated to the abuser's role` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the abuse happen in circumstances wholly unrelated to the abuser's association with the organisation (or the organisation the care was delegated to)?
      `the organisation proves it took reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the organisation prove, on the balance of probabilities, that it took reasonable precautions to prevent the abuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the organisation presumed to have breached its duty to prevent my abuse` `the day of the abuse` `my age at the abuse` `the abuse was` `it is the State of Victoria itself` `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` `it has care, supervision or authority over children` `its legal standing` `the abuser was` `the organisation is religious` `the only link is that the organisation funded or regulated another` `I was in its care, supervision or authority` `the abuse was wholly unrelated to the abuser's role` `the organisation proves it took reasonable precautions` MEANS
    `s 91 -- the organisation is presumed to have breached its duty` `the day of the abuse` `my age at the abuse` `the abuse was` (`s 88 -- the entity is a relevant organisation` `it is the State of Victoria itself` `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` `it has care, supervision or authority over children` `its legal standing`) (`s 90 -- the individual is associated with the organisation` `the abuser was` `the organisation is religious` `the only link is that the organisation funded or regulated another`) `I was in its care, supervision or authority` `the abuse was wholly unrelated to the abuser's role` `the organisation proves it took reasonable precautions`

@export Whom do I sue for the organisation's or institution's liability for my abuse (ss 91(5), 92, 93D)?
GIVEN `the organisation is` IS A `Kind of defendant` @desc Is it the State itself; a public sector body (or acting for the State) that can, or cannot, be sued; or another entity that can be sued, cannot be sued but has nominated a legal person, or cannot be sued and has nominated no one?
GIVETH AN `Appropriate defendant`
`Whom do I sue for my abuse` `the organisation is` MEANS
    `ss 91(5), 92, 93D -- the appropriate defendant` `the organisation is`

§§ `Statutory vicarious liability for child abuse (Part XIIIA)`
-- Situation: you were abused as a child, at any time, by an employee or someone akin to an employee of an institution.

@export Is the institution vicariously liable for my abuse by its employee or someone akin to an employee (s 93C)? Applies to abuse before, on or after 25 February 2026.
GIVEN `the institution is the State or a child-care organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the institution the State of Victoria, or a relevant organisation under s 88 (see that question)?
      `my age at the abuse` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age, in years, when the abuse happened
      `the abuse was` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc Was it sexual assault or other sexual misconduct, physical abuse, force with a lawful justification or excuse, or other harm?
      `the abuser was` IS AN `Abuser's relationship to the institution` @desc Was the abuser its employee; an individual a court would find akin to an employee (doing work integral to and for the benefit of the institution, under its control); an independent contractor; or someone else?
      `a court would find their role supplied the occasion for the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court find that the apparent performance of a role the institution placed them in (with authority, power or control over you, your trust, or the ability to achieve intimacy with you) supplied the occasion for the abuse?
      `they took advantage of that occasion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they take advantage of, or use, that occasion to abuse you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the institution vicariously liable for my abuse` `the institution is the State or a child-care organisation` `my age at the abuse` `the abuse was` `the abuser was` `a court would find their role supplied the occasion for the abuse` `they took advantage of that occasion` MEANS
    `s 93C -- the institution is vicariously liable for the abuse` `the institution is the State or a child-care organisation` `my age at the abuse` `the abuse was` `the abuser was` `a court would find their role supplied the occasion for the abuse` `they took advantage of that occasion`
